---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { buildBreadcrumbSchema, buildFAQSchema } from "../../lib/seo";

const pageFaqs = [
  {
    question: "How should I use this guide effectively?",
    answer: "Use the structure on one timed response, review where logic breaks, then revise the same response once. This loop builds score-related habits faster than writing many unchecked answers.",
  },
  {
    question: "Is this enough for a high band or CLB score?",
    answer: "This guide gives you a strong strategy baseline. Most candidates improve faster when they combine it with targeted lessons and feedback.",
  },
  {
    question: "What should I do after reading this page?",
    answer: "Practice one task immediately, then compare your draft against the checklist and linked resources below.",
  },
];

const pageStructuredData = [
  buildBreadcrumbSchema(Astro.site, [
    { name: "Home", path: "/" },
    { name: "Blog", path: "/blog/" },
    { name: "IELTS Listening Common Traps", path: "/blog/ielts-listening-common-traps/" },
  ]),
  buildFAQSchema(pageFaqs),
];
---

<Layout
  title="IELTS Listening Common Traps | How to Avoid Easy Score Loss"
  description="IELTS listening trap patterns and prevention strategies for distractors, corrections, spelling errors, and answer transfer mistakes."
  type="article"
  keywords="IELTS listening traps, IELTS listening mistakes, IELTS listening distractors"
  structuredData={pageStructuredData}
>
  <article class="section" style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto; padding-top: var(--s-6);">
    <div style="margin-bottom: var(--s-4);">
      <a href="/blog" style="color: var(--accent);">&larr; Back to blog</a>
    </div>

    <header style="margin-bottom: var(--s-4);">
      <h1 style="margin: 0;">IELTS Listening Common Traps</h1>
      <div style="display: flex; gap: var(--s-3); color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: var(--s-2); flex-wrap: wrap;">
        <span>March 14, 2026</span>
        <span>IELTS Corner Team</span>
        <span>6 min read</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="divider" style="margin: var(--s-4) 0; height: 2px; background: var(--text-muted-light);"></div>

    <div class="article-content" style="line-height: 1.8;">
      <p>Most listening score drops are predictable: distractor answers, corrected information, and weak checking habits. This page helps you neutralize those traps.</p>

      <h2>Quick strategy framework</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Plan before writing or speaking so your response has a clear structure.</li>
        <li>Keep one main idea per paragraph or answer block.</li>
        <li>Support claims with one relevant reason or example, not multiple weak points.</li>
        <li>Leave time for a short review step to catch avoidable errors.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Common mistakes to avoid</h2>
      <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: var(--s-3) 0;">
        <tr style="background: var(--surface);">
          <th style="text-align: left; padding: var(--s-2); border: 1px solid var(--text-muted-light);">Mistake</th>
          <th style="text-align: left; padding: var(--s-2); border: 1px solid var(--text-muted-light);">Better move</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td style="padding: var(--s-2); border: 1px solid var(--text-muted-light);">Starting without a plan</td>
          <td style="padding: var(--s-2); border: 1px solid var(--text-muted-light);">Take 1-2 minutes to map your response first.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td style="padding: var(--s-2); border: 1px solid var(--text-muted-light);">Adding ideas without development</td>
          <td style="padding: var(--s-2); border: 1px solid var(--text-muted-light);">Develop fewer ideas with clearer support.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td style="padding: var(--s-2); border: 1px solid var(--text-muted-light);">Skipping review</td>
          <td style="padding: var(--s-2); border: 1px solid var(--text-muted-light);">Reserve a short final check for clarity and errors.</td>
        </tr>
      </table>

      <h2>Related guides and next steps</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/ielts/listening">IELTS listening hub</a></li>
        <li><a href="/blog/ielts-listening-question-types">Listening question types guide</a></li>
        <li><a href="/lessons/ielts/listening">IELTS listening lessons</a></li>
        <li><a href="/tutoring">IELTS coaching</a></li>
      </ul>

      <h2>FAQ</h2>
      {pageFaqs.map((item) => (
        <details class="card" style="margin-bottom: var(--s-3);">
          <summary style="cursor: pointer; font-weight: 700;">{item.question}</summary>
          <p class="muted" style="margin-top: var(--s-2); margin-bottom: 0;">{item.answer}</p>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .article-content {
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .article-content h2 {
    margin-top: var(--s-5);
    margin-bottom: var(--s-2);
  }

  .article-content ul {
    margin: var(--s-2) 0;
    padding-left: var(--s-4);
  }

  .article-content li {
    margin: var(--s-1) 0;
  }
</style>

